// A dark two-level warren with two seeds in its dead ends, then two origins two cells apart on a trench floor whose echoes cancelled in the middle. Something above the shelf that the road does not lead to.
name Two Echoes
rule B1357/S1357
steps 3
hint Two seeds hide in this warren: one at the end of the low tunnel, one on the shelf above it, reached by the falling blocks. In the trench, two echoes crossed and cancelled where they met: a cell with an even count stays dark. Find where each began.
tip The shape is symmetric, but nothing began at its centre: that is where the two echoes cancelled. The stones are two cells apart on the floor, one either side of the middle, each right beside a lone floor cell.
intro Two origins, close enough to touch. Their echoes crossed, and where they crossed they cancelled, and the shape they left has a hole where you would look first.
outro Two beginnings, one shape. Nothing that grows keeps its own edges.
say wake|Two seeds, and this place hides both. Low first, then high. And the rock above the shelf is not as solid as it looks.
say seed|One. The other is above your head somewhere.
say plant|Two apart. Any closer and they are one echo; any further and they stop cancelling.
say grow|Watch the middle stay dark. That is two things agreeing to disappear.
say found|Cancelled and exact. Up the echo, past the vents.
say die|The vent counts to three and breathes. Count with it.
say secret|Nobody comes here. This is the first seed: the one everything else grew from. It is yours now, and so is my light. Look at it.
